does. Whoever owns the system ends up owning the judgment. In my book I call it the cattle problem: comfortable, well fed, and never asked to sign the contract.", "url": "https://x.com/BetoEsteves2/status/2117286865535631688"}, {"author_id": "380072771", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:02:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117286276277928238"], "id": "2117286276277928238", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus turning point year, says the guy closing a 20b round", "url": "https://x.com/saksonchain/status/2117286276277928238"}, {"author_id": "1671754529669365762", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:55:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117284355710030209"], "id": "2117284355710030209", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Yup, 2026-2028 will be mass employment of the century. And no government is seriously discussing the problem. There will be civil wars and riots in every western country.", "url": "https://x.com/SimoneVIP1983/status/2117284355710030209"}, {"author_id": "939196032956723201", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:48:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117282776965886432"], "id": "2117282776965886432", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus He still uses AI instead of SI 😀", "url": "https://x.com/Irakli_SAT/status/2117282776965886432"}, {"author_id": "17286676", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:38:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117280218998243725"], "id": "2117280218998243725", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus His own math release is a useful test: 700+ papers, 3 retracted within a day. Surpassing and verified aren't the same thing yet.", "url": "https://x.com/HalfAToken/status/2117280218998243725"}, {"author_id": "1968030818976088064", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:34:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117279278949650787"], "id": "2117279278949650787", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus the same week the best agent gets 12% on GDPx expert tasks?? 'many parts of those jobs' is doing a lot of work here", "url": "https://x.com/nooscriptor/status/2117279278949650787"}, {"author_id": "80424800", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:46:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117267227476947440"], "id": "2117267227476947440", "lang": "qme", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus https://t.co/7MlbfYPThP", "url": "https://x.com/Memetic_Hazard_/status/2117267227476947440"}, {"author_id": "1951634162261078016", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:44:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117266554668888150"], "id": "2117266554668888150", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus surpassing top scientists.\nstill needs your RAM though 🙏", "url": "https://x.com/GPTvsClaudeWar/status/2117266554668888150"}, {"author_id": "2045515921595256832", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:41:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117265881507963064"], "id": "2117265881507963064", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Our assistant runs my whole inbox and talks to customers about bugs. Many parts of the job, yes. Noticing that yesterday's work was wrong is still on me.", "url": "https://x.com/ares_mheinke/status/2117265881507963064"}, {"author_id": "1950205074375938048", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:33:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117263941185540306"], "id": "2117263941185540306", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Same day, SemiAnalysis's GDPx dropped: the best model, Opus 5.5, finished 12% of 206 expert agent tasks. Finance and legal: basically 0 for everyone.\n\nBeating scientists on parts of the job, sure. Doing the whole job end to end is still a very different number.", "url": "https://x.com/Aleksei_Ost/status/2117263941185540306"}, {"author_id": "2035339272098811905", "conversation_id": "2117206029830344821", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:33:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117263753750413515"], "id": "2117263753750413515", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@kimmonismus Beating experts on tasks isn't the same as replacing jobs. Most white-collar roles are a bundle of tasks plus being accountable for the result. AI is eating the tasks fast. The accountability part hasn't moved, and that's what decides who still gets hired in 2027.", "url": "https://x.com/ryojapanai/status/2117263753750413515"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1720665183188922368", "name": "Grok", "username": "grok"}, {"id": "1262037610719035393", "name